opened on Jan 19, 2026

Issue body actions

After performing a few migrations of older sites to newer Umbraco 17 sites, I've noticed that when importing Grids / Nested contents over to their respective V17 counterparts, Often times you'll see the newly created blocks come through as draft blocks.
What seems to be missing when comparing a Non draft and draft block in this instance is the "expose" Json object.

In my own situations, what i've ended up doing as a workaround is creating a method like so in the relevant PropertyTypeMigrator override:

    public override async Task<object?> MigrateAsync(
            IPropertyType propertyType,
                return migrated;

            // Ensure expose array exists
            if (root["expose"] is not JsonArray expose)
            {
                expose = new JsonArray();
                root["expose"] = expose;
            }

            // Existing expose keys
            var existing = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            foreach (var e in expose.OfType<JsonObject>())
            {
                var ck = e["contentKey"]?.GetValue<string>();
                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ck))
                    existing.Add(ck);
            }

            // Collect all content keys we should expose
            var toExpose = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

            // 1) From contentData (BlockItem content items)
            if (root["contentData"] is JsonArray contentData)
            {
                foreach (var cd in contentData.OfType<JsonObject>())
                {
                    var k = cd["key"]?.GetValue<string>();
                    if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(k))
                        toExpose.Add(k);
                }
            }

            // 2) From Layout (recursive)
            CollectContentKeysFromLayout(root, toExpose);

            // Add missing expose entries
            foreach (var key in toExpose)
            {
                if (existing.Contains(key)) continue;

                expose.Add(new JsonObject
                {
                    ["contentKey"] = key,
                    ["culture"] = null,
                    ["segment"] = null
                });
            }

            return migrated switch
            {
                string => root.ToJsonString(new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = false }),
                JsonNode => root,
                _ => migrated
            };
        }

        private static void CollectContentKeysFromLayout(JsonObject root, HashSet<string> keys)
        {
            if (root["Layout"] is not JsonObject layout)
                return;

            // Standard Block Grid layout key
            if (layout["Umbraco.BlockGrid"] is JsonArray blocks)
            {
                foreach (var b in blocks.OfType<JsonObject>())
                    CollectFromLayoutItem(b, keys);
            }
        }

However, I feel like this double checking of the exposures existence based on the state of the migrated block should probably be moved to the core flow?

Right now mine only sorts out the BlockGrids not the Blocklists

Thoughts?

