## Description

RuurdSpeak

opened on Feb 2, 2026

Issue body actions

### Which Umbraco version are you using?

17.1.0

### Bug summary

After upgrading from Umbraco 13 to 17 we noticed that some of our pages (doctypes) are no longer able to load the Umbraco blockgrid. When visiting the page in the content editor you see the grid for a couple of seconds and then it dissapears and an error shows stating: "One or more Block Types of this Block Editor is using a Element-Type that is configured to Vary By Culture or Vary By Segment. This is not supported on a Content item that does not vary by Culture or Segment.".

The block grid is loaded via a composition. The doctypes using this composition all have the varying by culture option turned on in the settings tab. I have 2 identical doctypes both using the exact same compositions and having the exact same settings, but one loads the grid and the other throws the error. I have double checked that they both have the EXACT same settings.

Our guess is that Umbraco 13 used to have an allow segmentations option there aswell (for Umbraco Engage) but that option is no longer there. We have also deleted TEMP folder in Umbraco and also obj and bin folders. We have cleared all caches build all interal indexes, rebuild al models etc. But we keep getting this error.

### Specifics

Its checked and happens in all browsers. I added some screenshots to show how its all configured and what it looks like in Umbraco.

### Steps to reproduce

Not sure if it would happen on a clean install. But this is what we have:

  * Make 2 doctypes for example for a textpage and a news page - set allow varying by culture on
  * Make a composition with a block grid, set allow varying by culture on
  * Add this composition to both of the doctypes
  * add a page for both of those doctypes in content tree
  * See if both show the grid, or if there is an error saying "One or more Block Types of this Block Editor is using a Element-Type that is configured to Vary By Culture or Vary By Segment. This is not supported on a Content item that does not vary by Culture or Segment."

### Expected result / actual result

There is no reason why its showing the error. It should show a working grid.

